  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "[\"Opposite flank is not separately photographed in this figure; approximate bilateral symmetry is an explicit inference from planispiral coiling and the ventral figure. Do not claim mirrored surface damage is observed.\", \"Minor fracture/wear details and fossil palette are artistic simplification. Exact septal sutures/internal chambers are not modeled. Current species synonymy is not independently revised here.\", \"Kevmin photograph is a DIFFERENT unidentified Dactylioceras sp., 40 mm from Germany, used only as secondary real-fossil visual context. Never assign its dimensions, damage, colour or locality to GSM26407.\"] {\"unit\": \"metre\", \"maximum_diameter_m\": 0.059, \"measurement_diameter_m\": 0.0578, \"whorl_height_m\": 0.0163, \"whorl_breadth_m\": 0.0164, \"umbilicus_width_m\": 0.0305, \"measurement_source\": \"p.115 actual dimensions in mm; definition/order p.95, NOT percentages. 59 mm maximum diameter; other values at 57.8 mm diameter. All figures natural size per p.110 caption. No measurement from rescaled PDF pixels.\", \"tolerance\": \"Low-poly design target: diameter 0.057–0.061 m; breadth about 0.015–0.018 m; umbilicus about 0.029–0.033 m. These are engineering tolerances, not biological uncertainty measurements.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：[\"Opposite flank is not separately photographed in this figure; approximate bilateral symmetry is an explicit inference from planispiral coiling and the ventral figure. Do not claim mirrored surface damage is observed.\", \"Minor fracture/wear details and fossil palette are artistic simplification. Exact septal sutures/internal chambers are not modeled. Current species synonymy is not independently revised here.\", \"Kevmin photograph is a DIFFERENT unidentified Dactylioceras sp., 40 mm from Germany, used only as secondary real-fossil visual context. Never assign its dimensions, damage, colour or locality to GSM26407.\"] {\"unit\": \"metre\", \"maximum_diameter_m\": 0.059, \"measurement_diameter_m\": 0.0578, \"whorl_height_m\": 0.0163, \"whorl_breadth_m\": 0.0164, \"umbilicus_width_m\": 0.0305, \"measurement_source\": \"p.115 actual dimensions in mm; definition/order p.95, NOT percentages. 59 mm maximum diameter; other values at 57.8 mm diameter. All figures natural size per p.110 caption. No measurement from rescaled PDF pixels.\", \"tolerance\": \"Low-poly design target: diameter 0.057–0.061 m; breadth about 0.015–0.018 m; umbilicus about 0.029–0.033 m. These are engineering tolerances, not biological uncertainty measurements.\"}"
